query) pointed out that the shell handles * expansion.

He than also went on to offer a method whereby we could do this:

tar cf $tape -C /dir1 `cd /dir1; ls file1*` -C /dir2 `cd /dir2; ls file2*` ...

Cheers,
T.
  


