OS: TRU64 5.1A
Problem: can't get C2 password checking


I used sysman secconfig to configure Enhanced Security:

Enhanced -> Custom -> AutoMigrate Users (left the rest as default) ->
segment sharing -> set root password -> Finish

I was instructed to reboot the machine, which i did.  At that point, I could
no longer login as root, or any local user.  I recycled power & init s.  The
passwd file was altered & showed '*' in the password field.  So I ran passwd
to verify root's passwd.  Once changed, it said no hash db, only updating
/etc/passwd.  Looking at /etc/passwd again, root's passwd field now has the
encrypted passwd, and all other accounts are still '*'.

No matter what I do, I can't figure out what step I'm missing to finish this
C2 passwd migration.  I can't login as users, but I can su - $USER.  if I
try to change the passwd as the user, the old password doesn't get verified
& I'm still SOL.

Any suggestions as to what I'm missing?  I'm following the Security document
on HP's website for 5.1A.

-Rob


