Ok:

         Lesson learned:  NEVER try to install an upgrade from a non-mount 
point.  You will hose you're cluster.  If I had created a tmp ADVFS file 
system and copied the contents of the CD onto the new filesystem it should 
work.  However, I don't think I'll try upgrading from anything other than 
the CDs again.

         Upgrade path from 5.1 to 5.1BPK should go something like 
this:  Rolling upgrade from 5.1 to 5.1A - this means the full 
procedure.  Then another rolling upgrade from 5.1A to 5.1B (but you can put 
down PK1 during this).

         Thanks for all the help everyone.

         Paul


